<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sets 1,000 lev/mark peg -- state radio.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sets 1,000 lev/mark peg -- state radio.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria will peg the national currency, the lev to the mark as anchor in a currency board system to be launched July 1 at a fixed exchange rate of 1,000, state radio quoted Finance Minister Muravei Radev as saying.</p>
<p>This year's budget deficit was assumed at 6.3 percent of projected Gross Domestic Product, up from 3.8 recommended by the International Monetary Fund in March.</p>
<p>Details will be announced at a joint news conference to be given by Radev and the IMF at 0930 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
</text>
